From 174cf5fb55ad06b6fbbbf4d8050ff4778befae63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vadik Likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 21:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: tegra-pkvm: export raw pvIOMMU stream IDs

Protected-device registration reads the endpoint directly from the device
tree and therefore records raw stream ID 6 for MGBE0.  When the pKVM Tegra
IOMMU driver probes first, its firmware specification contains the provider
stream-match mask packed above that ID.  Returning the packed value from
get_device_iommu_id() makes pvIOMMU route the guest's virtual SID to
0x7f800006, which cannot match the registered endpoint and fails the guest
attach with -EPERM.

Keep the stream-match mask at the Tegra SMMU hardware-routing boundary and
return the raw stream ID through the generic protected-device API.  This
keeps the endpoint identity consistent between protected-device registration
and pvIOMMU without weakening the masked SMR programmed by EL2.

Signed-off-by: Vadik Likholetov <vadikas@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
index e3a8bbd49..ac98d29ef 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm-smmu-tegra-pkvm.c
@@ -514,7 +514,7 @@ static int pkvm_tegra_device_id(struct device *dev, u32 idx,
 	if (idx >= fwspec->num_ids)
 		return -ENOENT;
 	*out_iommu = master->smmu->id;
-	*out_sid = fwspec->ids[idx];
+	*out_sid = FIELD_GET(PKVM_SMMU_SMR_ID, fwspec->ids[idx]);
 	return 0;
 }
 
